# Implementation Plan — Publication-Ready 500-Document Benchmark & Defect Remediation

This implementation plan details the technical fixes, validation protocol, dataset regeneration, execution strategy, and report generation required to conduct a publication-grade benchmark of the Academic Universe Document Intelligence Core (AU DIC Hybrid) against baseline systems.

---

## Technical Strategy & Architecture Overview

The previous official 500-document benchmark (`EXP-20260728212358`) successfully validated pipeline execution but uncovered three critical infrastructure defects that prevented valid statistical evaluation of SYS-PROP and SYS-BASE-3:

1. **Defect D1 (Format Constraint):** OpenRouter vision API rejects base64 PDFs (`application/pdf`) with HTTP 400.
2. **Defect D2 (Quota Limitation):** Gemini API free-tier rolling quota exhausted after sustained ~7h processing across prior systems, causing 429 cascades in SYS-PROP.
3. **Defect D3 (Category Tagging Defect):** `DatasetLoader.inferCategory()` defaulted all synthetic documents in `dataset/RAW` to `EDGE_CASE` instead of reading the true category from Ground Truth JSON metadata.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Component 1: Benchmark Core Pipeline & Infrastructure Defect Fixes

#### [MODIFY] [`datasetLoader.ts`](file:///C:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/benchmarks/dataset/datasetLoader.ts)
- **Fix Defect D3 (Category Propagation):** In `buildManifestFromDirectory()`, check if the Ground Truth JSON exists for each document (`ground-truth/${docId}.json`). If present, parse its `category` property directly rather than calling `inferCategory()`. This guarantees 100% accurate document category propagation into `dataset/manifest.json`.

#### [MODIFY] [`openRouterSingleRunner.ts`](file:///C:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/benchmarks/baselines/openRouterSingleRunner.ts) & [`academicUniverseDICRunner.ts`](file:///C:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/benchmarks/baselines/academicUniverseDICRunner.ts)
- **Fix Defect D1 (PNG Conversion for Vision API):** Update OpenRouter calls to convert incoming PDF buffers to PNG using `pdf-to-img` dynamically if `mimeType === 'application/pdf'`.
- Ensure base64 PNG data URL (`data:image/png;base64,...`) is sent to OpenRouter `/chat/completions`.

#### [MODIFY] [`pipelineExecutor.ts`](file:///C:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/benchmarks/runners/pipelineExecutor.ts) & [`benchmarkOrchestrator.ts`](file:///C:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/benchmarks/runners/pipelineExecutor.ts)
- **Fix Defect D2 (Rate Limiting & Inter-Request Throttle):** 
  - Increase inter-request delay to **2,500ms** between API requests.
  - Implement exponential backoff for HTTP 429 rate limit errors (up to 5 retries, initial delay 5,000ms, multiplier 2.0).
  - Increase inter-system cooldown in `BenchmarkOrchestrator` from **10s** to **30s** to allow rolling quota windows to clear.

---

### Component 2: Dataset Regeneration & Validation (Seed 100, n=500)

#### [MODIFY] [`generate500Dataset.ts`](file:///C:/github/academicuniverse.com/academicuniverse/benchmarks/scripts/generate500Dataset.ts)
- Regenerate deterministic 500-document dataset using `seed: 100`.
- Verify manifest integrity, SHA-256 checksums, and Ground Truth schema compliance.
- Confirm category breakdown across 11 standard academic categories (MARKSHEET, TRANSCRIPT, CERTIFICATE, WORKSHOP_CERTIFICATE, INTERNSHIP_CERTIFICATE, HACKATHON_CERTIFICATE, TIMETABLE, EXAM_TIMETABLE, ADMIT_CARD, FEE_RECEIPT, STUDENT_ID).

---

### Component 3: Execution & Statistical Analysis Pipeline

- Execute the complete 500-document benchmark across all 4 configured systems (`SYS-BASE-1`, `SYS-BASE-2`, `SYS-BASE-3`, `SYS-PROP`).
- Recompute all evaluation metrics:
  - Overall Precision, Recall, F1-Score
  - Per-field accuracy (studentName, rollNumber, semester, sgpa, cgpa, issueDate)
  - Per-category accuracy across all 11 categories
  - Latency statistics: Mean, Median (P50), P95, P99
  - Statistical significance tests (Wilcoxon signed-rank test, Cohen's d effect size ratings)

